                  "text": "•\tBuilt a Node.js web application as a platform for mentor-seeking and long-time mentor-mentee relationship maintenance by cooperating in a group of 4 and used GitHub for resource control.\n•\tUsed EJS template as view engine in front-end, and MongoDB as the database, add Mongoose module in the server side for data management, and built 5 schemas based on different requirements\n•\tFollowed 3-tier web architecture that has presentation layer, logic layer, and data layer, and each tier is separate with a clear interface between them.\n\n•\tUsed REST as an architectural style and used Express to build several separate routes.\n•\tImplemented a private chatroom using Socket.io, which can show the online/offline status and store the chat logs in database \n•\tUsed Passport module for local and third-party authentication, and used Bcrypt module to encode user password by hash algorithm and store the hashed value in the database.\n•\tApplied Connect Flash module to show the login and register hints as a helper for Passport module.\n•\tRealized file uploads using Formidable module.\n"
